<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottoman Hungary</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1541">1541</a>–<a href="/years/1699">1699</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> was the central and southern part of the medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a> ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> from the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buda">Buda</a> in 1541 until the reconquest of the 1680s and 1690s. Organised mainly in the eyalets of Buda and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timisoara">Temesvár</a>, it was a frontier zone of fortresses and depopulated plains. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-karlowitz">Treaty of Karlowitz</a> of 1699 confirmed its loss to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, except the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banat">Banat</a> of Temesvár, taken in 1716–1718.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ottoman-hungary.jpg" alt="Ottoman Hungary" width="320" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: WikiEditor2004 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Central_europe_1683.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Two rival kings were elected, John Zápolya in November and Ferdinand I of Habsburg in December 1526, and after the Ottoman seizure of Buda in 1541 the kingdom was divided into Habsburg Royal Hungary, <b>Ottoman Hungary</b> and the Principality of Transylvania.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1301-1526">Kingdom of Hungary (1301-1526) · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The division between Habsburg Royal Hungary, <b>Ottoman Hungary</b> and Transylvania lasted until the late 17th century.</blockquote><a href="/state/eastern-hungarian-kingdom">Eastern Hungarian Kingdom</a></li></ul></section>
